{% comment %}
  Legal document body. Privacy Policy and Terms & Conditions.

  BLOCKS, NOT ONE RICHTEXT FIELD. Shopify's richtext setting permits only
  <p>, <br>, <strong>, <em> and <a> -- it cannot produce the headings and
  lists a legal document is made of. So the document's STRUCTURE is blocks and
  only the prose inside each one is richtext.

  That also means the merchant can rewrite this in the theme editor without
  touching the repo, which is the point: the copy here is placeholder and is
  expected to be replaced by real policy text.

  THE CONTENT IS PLACEHOLDER. Lorem ipsum from the mockup, in place so the
  layout can be built and checked at every width. It is NOT legal copy and
  must not ship to a live page handle. See docs/redesign-open-items.md.

  LIST ITEMS carry an optional bold lead-in, written before a pipe:

      Service providers.|Ut et voluptates repudiandae sint...

  renders as "<b>Service providers.</b> Ut et voluptates...". One item per
  line. Everything is escaped, so the pipe is the only markup a merchant can
  write here and there is no way to inject HTML through a list.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle -%}

{%- comment -%}
  CONTINUES A SECTION ABOVE IT. A long document has to be split across two
  instances of this section, because Shopify caps a SECTION at 50 blocks --
  not a page. Splitting is the only way past that ceiling, and it costs a seam:
  .suf-section carries padding-block, so two stacked instances double it and
  the document visibly breaks in half.

  This zeroes the top padding on the continuation so the two read as one
  document. Same idea as suf-cert's flush_top, and named to match.

  NO HAIRLINE SEAM HERE, unlike suf-cert. That one joins two navy bands and
  needs the rule to stay legible as two things. This is body copy on the page
  background, where a rule would announce a division that does not exist -- the
  split is an implementation detail of the block cap, not part of the document.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign section_classes = 'suf-section' -%}
{%- if section.settings.continues -%}
  {%- assign section_classes = section_classes | append: ' suf-section--legal-continues' -%}
{%- endif -%}

<div class="{{ section_classes }}" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <div class="suf-legal">
      {%- if section.settings.updated != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A <p>, not a <time>: the value is merchant-typed prose ("August 27,
          2026") with no machine-readable datetime to pair with it, and a
          <time> without a datetime attribute is worth nothing to anything
          reading the page.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="suf-legal__updated">{{ section.settings.updated | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.lead != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A <div>, not a <p>: a richtext setting emits its own <p>, and
          nesting one inside another is invalid -- the browser auto-closes the
          outer element and the content escapes the styled wrapper.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="suf-legal__lead">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.lead %}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- case block.type -%}
          {%- when 'heading' -%}
            <h2 {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- assign heading = block.settings.text | escape -%}
              {%- render 'suf-nb', text: heading -%}
            </h2>

          {%- when 'subheading' -%}
            <h3 {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- assign subheading = block.settings.text | escape -%}
              {%- render 'suf-nb', text: subheading -%}
            </h3>

          {%- when 'text' -%}
            <div class="suf-legal__prose" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- render 'suf-nb', text: block.settings.text -%}
            </div>

          {%- when 'list' -%}
            {%- assign items = block.settings.items | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- if items.size > 0 -%}
              {%- if block.settings.numbered -%}
                <ol {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- else -%}
                <ul {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- for item in items -%}
                {%- assign line = item | strip -%}
                {%- if line != blank -%}
                  <li>
                    {%- comment -%}
                      `contains` first: split always returns at least one part,
                      so testing parts.size cannot tell a lead-in from a plain
                      line.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- if line contains '|' -%}
                      {%- assign parts = line | split: '|' -%}
                      {%- assign label = parts[0] | strip | escape -%}
                      {%- assign rest = parts | slice: 1, 99 | join: '|' | strip | escape -%}
                      <b>{% render 'suf-nb', text: label %}</b>
                      {{ ' ' }}{% render 'suf-nb', text: rest %}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- assign line = line | escape -%}
                      {%- render 'suf-nb', text: line -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}

              {%- if block.settings.numbered -%}
                </ol>
              {%- else -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Legal document (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 50,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Anchor id" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "continues",
      "label": "Continues the section above",
      "info": "For a document long enough to need two of these sections -- a section is capped at 50 blocks. Zeroes the top padding so the two read as one document. Leave the heading numbering running on, and leave \"Last updated\" and the opening paragraph on the FIRST one only.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "updated",
      "label": "Last updated",
      "info": "e.g. \"Last updated: August 27, 2026\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Opening paragraph",
      "info": "Set larger than the body copy. One paragraph."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "name": "Section heading",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Heading", "info": "Numbered by hand, e.g. \"1. Introduction\"." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "subheading",
      "name": "Sub-heading",
      "settings": [{ "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Sub-heading" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "name": "Paragraph",
      "settings": [{ "type": "richtext", "id": "text", "label": "Text" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "name": "List",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "items",
          "label": "Items",
          "info": "One per line. For a bold lead-in, put it before a pipe: \"Refunds.|Text of the item\"."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "numbered",
          "label": "Numbered",
          "info": "Off renders the slash bullets; on renders red numerals.",
          "default": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Legal document (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "heading" }, { "type": "text" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
